I have implemented the requested functionality to allow admins to change a user's role directly from the users list. 

Here is a summary of the changes:

### 1. New API Hook (`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/api/update-user-role.ts`)
Created a new mutation hook `useUpdateUserRole` that performs the `PATCH /users/{userId}/role` request. On success, it invalidates the users query (to refetch the list and show the new role) and triggers a success notification.

### 2. Role Select Component (`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/components/update-user-role.tsx`)
Created `UpdateUserRole`, a lightweight component that renders a native `<select>` dropdown. It uses the `useUpdateUserRole` hook to handle state changes and disables the select while the request is pending.

### 3. Updated Users List (`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/components/users-list.tsx`)
Updated the `Table` component's "Role" column to render the new `UpdateUserRole` component instead of plain text. This allows in-cell editing and integrates seamlessly with the existing table structure.

### Code Changes

**`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/api/update-user-role.ts`** (New file)
```typescript
import { useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';

import { useNotifications } from '@/components/ui/notifications';
import { api } from '@/lib/api-client';
import { MutationConfig } from '@/lib/react-query';

import { getUsersQueryOptions } from './get-users';

export type UpdateUserRoleDTO = {
  userId: string;
  role: 'ADMIN' | 'USER';
};

export const updateUserRole = ({ userId, role }: UpdateUserRoleDTO) => {
  return api.patch(`/users/${userId}/role`, { role });
};

type UseUpdateUserRoleOptions = {
  mutationConfig?: MutationConfig<typeof updateUserRole>;
};

export const useUpdateUserRole = ({
  mutationConfig,
}: UseUpdateUserRoleOptions = {}) => {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  const { onSuccess, ...restConfig } = mutationConfig || {};

  return useMutation({
    onSuccess: (data, variables, context) => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({
        queryKey: getUsersQueryOptions().queryKey,
      });

      useNotifications.getState().addNotification({
        type: 'success',
        title: 'Success',
        message: `User role updated to ${variables.role}`,
      });

      onSuccess?.(data, variables, context);
    },
    ...restConfig,
    mutationFn: updateUserRole,
  });
};
```

**`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/components/update-user-role.tsx`** (New file)
```tsx
import { useUpdateUserRole } from '../api/update-user-role';

interface UpdateUserRoleProps {
  userId: string;
  currentRole: 'ADMIN' | 'USER';
}

export const UpdateUserRole = ({ userId, currentRole }: UpdateUserRoleProps) => {
  const updateRoleMutation = useUpdateUserRole();

  const handleRoleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLSelectElement>) => {
    const newRole = e.target.value as 'ADMIN' | 'USER';
    updateRoleMutation.mutate({ userId, role: newRole });
  };

  return (
    <select
      value={currentRole}
      onChange={handleRoleChange}
      disabled={updateRoleMutation.isPending}
      className="cursor-pointer rounded border-gray-300 bg-white p-1 text-sm text-gray-700 focus:border-indigo-500 focus:ring-indigo-500"
    >
      <option value="ADMIN">Admin</option>
      <option value="USER">User</option>
    </select>
  );
};
```

